```ts
export function pageBounds(total: number, page: number, size: number): { start: number; end: number } {
  const pages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(total / size));
  const capped = Math.min(Math.max(page, 1), pages);
  return { start: (capped - 1) * size, end: Math.min(total, capped * size) };
}
```

Nothing here needs a new dependency, so the change stays inside the module. I moved the magic number into a named constant so the next reader does not have to guess its unit. The order of the items is the thing that makes the cursor stable, so the sort stays before the slice. The old code copied the whole array on every call; the new one copies only the page.

